# Cosmos DB — EF Core 9 Breaking Change Fixes

Apply these patterns in your **separate Cosmos DB project** after upgrading
its packages to `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Cosmos` **9.0.x**.

---

## Fix 1 — Discriminator property renamed from `"Discriminator"` → `"$type"`

Existing documents use `"Discriminator"`. Explicitly configure to keep the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Session>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

## Fix 2 — `id` property no longer includes the discriminator

EF Core 8 stored id as `"Session|123"`. EF Core 9 stores just `"123"`.
Preserve the old compound format so existing documents remain accessible:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Session>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

## Fix 3 — Synchronous I/O now throws

Sync methods (`ToList()`, `SaveChanges()`, etc.) on the Cosmos provider now
throw at runtime. Replace **all** sync calls with async equivalents:

```csharp
// BREAKS in EF Core 9:
var sessions = db.Sessions.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// Fix:
var sessions = await db.Sessions.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```

